If a patient has a combined-opioid-dosage and the combined-opioid-dosage includes at least 50 MME-units-per-day then every clinician should increase a follow-up-frequency for the patient and should offer a naloxone-dose to the patient and should provide an opioid-overdose-education to the patient.
If a patient has a combined-opioid-dosage and the combined-opioid-dosage includes at least 50 MME-units-per-day and the patient has a household-member then every clinician should offer a naloxone-dose to the household-member and should provide an opioid-overdose-education to the household-member.
